„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter	¨sectionsš…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ/And when the queen of Sheba heard of the fame of Solomon, she came to prove Solomon with hard questions at Jerusalem, with a very great company, and camels that bare spices, and gold in abundance, and precious stones: and when she was come to Solomon, she communed with him of all that was in her heart.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeAnd Solomon told her all her questions: and there was nothing hid from Solomon which he told her not.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\And when the queen of Sheba had seen the wisdom of Solomon, and the house that he had built,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙûand the meat of his table, and the sitting of his servants, and the attendance of his ministers, and their apparel; his cupbearers also, and their apparel; and his ascent by which he went up into the house of the LORD; there was no more spirit in her.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd she said to the king, It was a true report which I heard in mine own land of thine acts, and of thy wisdom:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÀhowbeit I believed not their words, until I came, and mine eyes had seen it: and, behold, the one half of the greatness of thy wisdom was not told me: for thou exceedest the fame that I heard.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnHappy are thy men, and happy are these thy servants, which stand continually before thee, and hear thy wisdom.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙíBlessed be the LORD thy God, which delighted in thee to set thee on his throne, to be king for the LORD thy God: because thy God loved Israel, to establish them for ever, therefore made he