„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂAnd the king made of the algum trees terraces to the house of the LORD, and to the king's palace, and harps and psalteries for singers: and there were none such seen before in the land of Judah.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÆAnd king Solomon gave to the queen of Sheba all her desire, whatsoever she asked, beside that which she had brought unto the king. So she turned, and went away to her own land, she and her servants.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoNow the weight of gold that came to Solomon in one year was six hundred and threescore and six talents of gold;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbeside that which chapmen and merchants brought. And all the kings of Arabia and governors of the country brought gold and silver to Solomon.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd king Solomon made two hundred targets of beaten gold: six hundred shekels of beaten gold went to one target.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ And three hundred shields made he of beaten gold: three hundred shekels of gold went to one shield. And the king put them in the house of the forest of Lebanon.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOMoreover the king made a great throne of ivory, and overlaid it with pure gold.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶And there were six steps to the throne, with a footstool of gold, which were fastened to the throne, and stays on each side of the sitting place, and two lions standing by the stays:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}and twelve lions stood there on the one side and on the other upon the six steps. There was not the like made in any kingdom.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖAnd all the drinking vessels of king Solomon were of gold, and all the vessels of the house of the forest of Lebanon were of pure gold: none were of silver; it was not any thing accounted of in the days of Solomon.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­For the king's ships went to Tarshish with the servants of Huram: every three years once came the ships of Tarshish bringing gold, and silver, ivory, and apes, and peacocks.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd king Solomon passed all the kings of the earth in riches and wisdom.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd all the kings of the earth sought the presence of Solomon, to hear his wisdom, that God had put in his heart.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™And they brought every man his present, vessels of silver, and vessels of gold, and raiment, harness, and spices, horses, and mules, a rate year by year.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ£And Solomon had four thousand stalls for horses and chariots, and twelve thousand horsemen; whom he bestowed in the chariot cities, and with the king at Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsAnd he reigned over all the kings from the river even unto the land of the Philistines, and to the border of Egypt.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‡And the king made silver in Jerusalem as stones, and cedar trees made he as the sycomore trees that are in the low plains in abundance.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHAnd they brought unto Solomon horses out of Egypt, and out of all lands.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙàNow the rest of the acts of Solomon, first and last, are they not written 